 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: ask\n\n  - id: checkout.cart.alternate\n    title: Update cart quantity before purchase\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: core\n    journey_role: alternate\n    usage_frequency: common\n    tags: [checkout, cart]\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: src/checkout/cart.ts\n    actor: buyer\n    intent: Change the cart before buying.\n    preconditions:\n      - The cart contains two items.\n    trigger: The buyer changes a quantity.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: checkout.cart.alternate.quantity\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Open the cart.\n          - Increase an item quantity.\n          - Review the updated total.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The total reflects the new quantity.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - The total reflects the new quantity.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: live_demo\n          required_verifiers: [user]\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: predefined\n      requirements:\n        - approver_type: user\n          minimum_count: 1\n      statement: User confirms the cart behavior is acceptable.\n\n  - id: checkout.validation.edge\n    title: Preserve cart after address validation\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: core\n    journey_role: edge\n    usage_frequency: occasional\n    tags: [checkout, validation]\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: src/checkout/address.ts\n    actor: buyer\n    intent: Recover from a validation error without losing cart state.\n    preconditions:\n      - The cart contains an in-stock item.\n    trigger: The buyer submits an invalid postcode.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: checkout.validation.edge.postcode\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Submit an invalid postcode.\n          - Correct the postcode.\n          - Continue checkout.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The cart contents remain unchanged.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - The cart contents remain unchanged.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: live_demo\n          required_verifiers: [user]\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: ask\n\n  - id: checkout.payment.negative\n    title: Declined card shows recovery path\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: core\n    journey_role: negative\n    usage_frequency: occasional\n    tags: [checkout, payment]\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: src/checkout/payment.ts\n    actor: buyer\n    intent: See a clear recovery path when payment fails.\n    preconditions:\n      - The buyer has a declined card.\n    trigger: The buyer submits the declined card.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: checkout.payment.negative.decline\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Submit a declined card.\n          - Read the recovery message.\n          - Choose another payment method.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The payment failure message is visible.\n          - The cart remains payable.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - The payment failure message is visible.\n      - The cart remains payable.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: live_demo\n          required_verifiers: [user]\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: ask\n\n  - id: checkout.inventory.failure\n    title: Sold-out item blocks order cleanly\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: supporting\n    journey_role: failure\n    usage_frequency: rare\n    tags: [checkout, inventory]\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: src/checkout/inventory.ts\n    actor: buyer\n    intent: Understand why an unavailable item cannot be bought.\n    preconditions:\n      - A cart item becomes sold out.\n    trigger: The buyer attempts to place the order.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: checkout.inventory.failure.soldout\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Attempt to buy a sold-out item.\n          - Remove the sold-out item.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The order is blocked with a sold-out explanation.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - The order is blocked with a sold-out explanation.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: live_demo\n          required_verifiers: [user]\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: ask\n"},{"kind":"file","path":"use-cases/settings.yml","text":"schema_version: 1\nfeature:\n  id: settings\n  name: Settings\n  summary: Users can personalize account preferences.\nuse_cases:\n  - id: settings.theme.rare\n    title: Switch to a seasonal theme\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: long_tail\n    journey_role: golden\n    usage_frequency: rare\n    tags: [settings, theme]\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: src/settings/theme.ts\n    actor: registered_user\n    intent: Apply a seasonal account theme.\n    preconditions:\n      - The user is signed in.\n    trigger: The user chooses a seasonal theme.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: settings.theme.rare.seasonal\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Open settings.\n          - Select the seasonal theme.\n          - Save the preference.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The seasonal theme is applied.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - The seasonal theme is applied.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      requirements:\n        - e