never quotable as acceptance.","An UNBOUND row is never counted as proven, so a matrix with unbound rows cannot claim acceptance.","The summary counts the local axis (verified / stale / unverified) alongside the signed axis, so a green keyless matrix does not read as a failing one."],"teardown_steps":[],"required_permissions":[],"safety_constraints":[],"verification_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"requirements","verifiers":{"script":{"kind":"script","evidence_kind":"test_result","command":["pnpm","-s","vitest","run","tests/blackbox/lifecycle-signals.test.ts","-t","lifecycle.signals.acceptance_claim_is_honest"],"inputs":["tests/blackbox/lifecycle-signals.test.ts"]}},"requirements":[{"evidence_kind":"test_result","required_verifiers":["script"],"minimum_count":1}]},"approval_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"none"},"approval_resolution_required_at_run_start":false,"required_evidence":[{"evidence_kind":"test_result","required_verifiers":["script"],"minimum_count":1,"status":"missing"}],"evidence_summary":{"readiness":"missing","active_evidence_ids":[],"basis":"no_active_evidence"},"freshness_summary":{"state":"unknown","basis":"missing_evidence"},"known_gaps":[{"code":"evidence_missing","message":"Required evidence is missing; live performance is still required.","severity":"warning"}],"selection_reasons":["Critical value use case.","Golden journey coverage.","Common usage frequency."],"selection_reason_codes":["value_critical","journey_golden","frequency_common"],"score_components":{"changed":0,"value":400,"journey":50,"frequency":30}},{"plan_item_id":"item.lifecycle.signals.local_results_are_attested","presentation_format":"reviewing","delivery_kind":"evidence_review","scenario_scope":"explicit","use_case_id":"lifecycle.signals.local_results_are_attested","use_case_title":"A verification result must prove a run wrote it","scenario_ids":["lifecycle.signals.local_results_are_attested.golden_real_run","lifecycle.signals.local_results_are_attested.bad_typed_line","lifecycle.signals.local_results_are_attested.bad_edited_record","lifecycle.signals.local_results_are_attested.edge_ledger_from_another_machine","lifecycle.signals.local_results_are_attested.edge_scan_never_mints_a_key"],"use_case_content_hash":"sha256:80656ac52d628aaad094f037b31ab9dd4b424f8fbb052254cabe7b538282830c","estimated_seconds":180,"estimate_source":"default_profile","setup_steps":[],"resolved_steps":["Run uc verify for a bound row so the verifier is actually spawned.","Read the emitted record, then scan and read the row's local status.","Hand-write a results line whose hashes all match the current code.","Scan and read the row's local status and the acceptance claim.","Take a genuine attested record of a FAILED run and edit its status to pass.","Scan and read whether the row is proven.","Copy in a results ledger attested with a different machine's key.","Scan and read the row's local status.","Remove the machine-local run key and run scan on a repo with no key present.","Check whether a key file appeared."],"expected_observations":["A record uc verify wrote carries a run attestation and reads VERIFIED_LOCAL.","Every record the tool emits carries an attestation, not only the passing ones.","A hand-written record with byte-perfect hashes reads UNATTESTED_LOCAL and is never counted as proven.","Matching hashes alone never move the claim, because anything that can read the repo can compute them.","Editing any field of an attested record, including flipping a failure to a pass, invalidates its attestation.","A laundered failure proves nothing.","A results ledger written on another machine reads unattested here, because someone else's run is not your evidence.","Scan never mints a key: a read-only command cannot attest anything.","A read-only command leaves no new key on disk.","A record `uc verify` wrote carries a run attestation and reads VERIFIED_LOCAL.","Editing any field of an attested record \u2014 including flipping a failure to a pass \u2014 invalidates its attestation."],"teardown_steps":[],"required_permissions":[],"safety_constraints":[],"verification_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"requirements","verifiers":{"script":{"kind":"script","evidence_kind":"test_result","command":["pnpm","-s","vitest","run","tests/blackbox/lifecycle-signals.test.ts","-t","lifecycle.signals.local_results_are_attested"],"inputs":["tests/blackbox/lifecycle-signals.test.ts"]}},"requirements":[{"evidence_kind":"test_result","required_verifiers":["script"],"minimum_count":1}]},"approval_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"none"},"approval_resolution_required_at_run_start":false,"required_evidence":[{"evidence_kind":"test_result","required_verifiers":["script"],"minimum_count":1,"status":"missing"}],"evidence_summary":{"readiness":"missing","active_evidence_ids":[],"basis":"no_active_evidence"},"freshness_summary":{"state":"unknown","basis":"missing_evidence"},"known_gaps":[{"code":"evidence_missing","message":"Required evidence is missing; live performance is still required.","severity":"warning"}],"selection_reasons":["Critical value use case.","Golden journey coverage.","Common usage frequency."],"selection_reason_codes":["value_critical","journey_golden","frequency_common"],"score_components":{"changed":0,"value":400,"journey":50,"frequency":30}},{"plan_item_id":"item.lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count","presentation_format":"reviewing","delivery_kind":"evidence_review","scenario_scope":"explicit","use_case_id":"lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count","use_case_title":"A run the tool drove counts, and a self-reported one does not","scenario_ids":["lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count.golden_driven","lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count.bad_self_reported","lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count.bad_observed_command_is_not_a_run","lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count.bad_failing_run_proves_nothing","lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count.bad_voided_record_does_not_count","lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count.edge_row_edited_after_the_run","lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count.edge_unbound_row_cannot_be_driven_into_proof","lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count.edge_same_row_driven_twice"],"use_case_content_hash":"sha256:6943e6aa0ad60fcd94fa13e2f4883dd01239ca5dcbc6dfc580670d315d385cc8","estimated_seconds":180,"estimate_source":"default_profile","setup_steps":[],"resolved_steps":["Drive the behaviour with uc evidence record --perform -- <cmd>.","Scan and read the acceptance claim.","Record a self-reported observation with no --perform.","Scan and read the acceptance claim.","Record a claim that names a full command line the tool merely watched, rather than executed.","Scan and read whether it counts.","Drive a behaviour with --perform where the command exits nonzero.","Scan and read whether the row is proven.","Drive a behaviour, then void the resulting evidence record.","Scan and read whether it still counts.","Drive a behaviour, then edit the row it proved.","Scan and read whether the run still counts.","Drive a command and name an UNBOUND row as its target.","Scan and read whether the row is proven.","Drive the same row twice with --perform.","Read how many performed runs the claim reports for it."],"expected_observations":["A tool-executed passing run proves its row, and the claim counts it under performed_run.","A self-reported record proves nothing, whatever it says.","Confidence in the summary text moves no number.","A record naming a command it merely observed is not a run the tool executed and does not count.","A structured claim with no argv does not count either.","A failing run does not prove the behaviour holds.","A voided record does not count.","Editing the row invalidates the run that proved the old one, so this tier decays like every other.","A run recorded against a row that has since left the matrix does not count.","An unbound row cannot be proven by driving something and naming it.","One row driven twice is reported once, so repetition never inflates the claim."],"teardown_steps":[],"required_permissions":[],"safety_constraints":[],"verification_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"requirements","verifiers":{"script":{"kind":"script","evidence_kind":"test_result","command":["pnpm","-s","vitest","run","tests/blackbox/lifecycle-signals.test.ts","-t","lifecycle.signals.performed_runs_count"],"inputs":["tests/blackbox/lifecycle-signals.test.ts"]}},"requirements":[{"evidence_kind":"test_result","required_verifiers":["script"],"minimum_count":1}]},"approval_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"none"},"approval_resolution_required_at_run_start":false,"required_evidence":[{"evidence_kind":"test_result","required_verifiers":["script"],"minimum_count":1,"status":"missing"}],"evidence_summary":{"readiness":"missing","active_evidence_ids":[],"basis":"no_active_evidence"},"freshness_summary":{"state":"unknown","basis":"missing_evidence"},"known_gaps":[{"code":"evidence_missing","message":"Required evidence is missing; live performance is still required.","severity":"warning"}],"selection_reasons":["Critical value use case.","Golden journey coverage.","Common usage frequency."],"selection_reason_codes":["value_critical","journey_golden","frequency_common"],"score_components":{"changed":0,"value":400,"journey":50,"frequency":30}},{"plan_item_id":"item.lifecycle.signals.verify_preserves_other_rows","presentation_format":"reviewing","delivery_kind":"evidence_review","scenario_scope":"explicit","use_case_id":"lifecycle.signals.verify_preserves_other_rows","use_case_title":"Verifying one row never destroys another row's evidence","scenario_ids":["lifecycle.signals.verify_preserves_other_rows.golden_single_row","lifecycle.signals.verify_preserves_other_rows.golden_replaces_prior_record","lifecycle.signals.verify_preserves_other_rows.bad_retained_evidence_is_rechecked","lifecycle.signals.verify_preserves_other_rows.edge_no_targets"],"use_case_content_hash":"sha256:0f167327e92b6db12ac5939557af98b048c0d2c9f94b5ae94b2e7295475f503a","estimated_seconds":180,"estimate_source":"default_profile","setup_steps":[],"resolved_steps":["Verify every bound row, so the results ledger holds a record for each.","Verify only ONE row against the same ledger.","Scan and read each row's local status.","Verify one bound row twice in succession against the same ledger.","Read the ledger and count the records carrying that row id.","Verify every bound row so each has a passing record.","Change the code inside ANOTHER row's bound span without re-verifying it.","Verify one unrelated row, then scan and read the changed row's local status.","Verify a row that is UNBOUND, so the run targets nothing at all.","Confirm the ledger is untouched rather than emptied."],"expected_observations":["Rows the run did not target keep their local evidence and stay VERIFIED_LOCAL.","The targeted row is re-verified and reads VERIFIED_LOCAL on the same ledger.","A re-verified row's prior record is replaced, never duplicated.","The ledger holds exactly one record per row id after the second run.","Retained evidence is still re-checked against the current code, so a row whose code changed is demoted to STALE_LOCAL rather than left falsely green.","Preserving a record is never the same as trusting it.","A run that targets no rows writes nothing away.","Every pre-existing record survives a run that matched nothing."],"teardown_steps":[],"required_permissions":[],"safety_constraints":[],"verification_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"requirements","verifiers":{"script":{"kind":"script","evidence_kind":"test_result","command":["pnpm","-s","vitest","run","tests/blackbox/lifecycle-signals.test.ts","-t","lifecycle.signals.verify_preserves_other_rows"],"inputs":["tests/blackbox/lifecycle-signals.test.ts"]}},"requirements":[{"evidence_kind":"test_result","required_verifiers":["script"],"minimum_count":1}]},"approval_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"none"},"approval_resolution_required_at_run_start":false,"required_evidence":[{"evidence_kind":"test_result","required_verifiers":["script"],"minimum_count":1,"status":"missing"}],"evidence_summary":{"readiness":"missing","active_evidence_ids":[],"basis":"no_active_evidence"},"freshness_summary":{"state":"unknown","basis":"missing_evidence"},"known_gaps":[{"code":"evidence_missing","message":"Required evidence is missing; live performance is still required.","severity":"warning"}],"selection_reasons":["Critical value use case.","Golden journey coverage.","Common usage frequency."],"selection_reason_codes":["value_critical","journey_golden","frequency_common"],"score_components":{"changed":0,"value":400,"journey":50,"frequency":30}},{"plan_item_id":"item.matrix.product.product_inventory","presentation_format":"reviewing","delivery_kind":"evidence_review","scenario_scope":"explicit","use_case_id":"matrix.product.product_inventory","use_case_title":"Living product behavior inventory","scenario_ids":["matrix.product.product_inventory.golden_cli","matrix.product.product_inventory.edge_primitive_rows_stay_supporting"],"use_case_content_hash":"sha256:7864fcabf3ca4302d9dae5c7b2f804e2b087929ee338571360da066634db8286","estimated_seconds":180,"estimate_source":"default_profile","setup_steps":[],"resolved_steps":["Run matrix list.","Confirm product-level rows exist alongside primitive support rows.","Confirm each row carries value, journey, usage and scenario data.","List the rows and separate product-level from primitive ones.","Read how each is presented."],"expected_observations":["Product behaviour can be selected by row id without reading implementation code.","Primitive rows remain available as supporting proof rather than the whole product map.","Product behavior can be selected by row ID without reading implementation code."],"teardown_steps":[],"required_permissions":[],"safety_constraints":[],"verification_policy_snapshot":{"mode":"requirements","verifiers":{"script":{"kind":"script","evidence_kind":"test_result","command":["pnpm","-s","vitest","run","tests/blackbox/matrix-product-inventory.test.ts","-t","matrix.product.product_inventory"],"inputs":["tests/bl